SimpleX auto-accept never accepted anything. Three bugs in one path;
each one alone leaves the peer at "contact should accept", unable to send.

1. THE BRANCH NEVER RAN. The adapter matched

       resp_type == "contactRequest"

   but that is the record FIELD carrying the request; the daemon emits the
   EVENT tag `receivedContactRequest`, from CEvtReceivedContactRequest
   (Controller.hs:877) via sumTypeJSON over dropPrefix "CEvt"
   (Controller.hs:1770). Observed on the wire against simplex-chat 7.0.0
   with two daemons and a real connection request:

       EVENT type = 'receivedContactRequest'
         keys: ['chat_', 'contactRequest', 'type', 'user']
         contactRequest.contactRequestId = 1
         ADAPTER MATCHES 'contactRequest'?  False

   No occurrence of "receivedContactRequest" exists in the adapter,
   v2026.8.3 included.

2. THE COMMAND WAS THE BY-NAME FORM. simplex-chat parses `/accept` as

       ("/accept" <|> "/ac") *> (AcceptContact <$> incognitoP
                                 <* A.space <* char_ '@' <*> displayNameP)

   (Commands.hs:5269), so `/accept 3` looks up a contact whose display
   NAME is "3" and answers

       contactRequestNotFoundByName {"contactName": "3"}

   The id form is a separate command, `/_accept <id>`
   (Commands.hs:5044), which answers `contactRequestNotFound
   {"contactRequestId": ...}` for a missing id - so it is the one that
   reads the argument as an id. Both probed against the same daemon.

3. AWAITING THE REPLY IN THE DISPATCH LOOP DEADLOCKS. _handle_event runs
   inside `async for raw in ws`, and _send_command registers a future that
   only that same loop can resolve. Awaiting it from inside the handler
   stalls the loop for the full 30s timeout; the reply is then read as an
   uncorrelated event and dropped. Live journal:

       SimpleX: command timed out: /_accept 3

   The accept itself still reached the daemon (the contact went
   activeConn PRESENT), so this bug does not block the connection - but
   it blinds the error path, stalls every other event behind it, and the
   30s window is a reconnect risk. The rcvFileDescrReady branch a few
   lines below already avoids this with _send_fire_and_forget; accept
   needs the response for its error path, so it gets a task instead.

Consequence of 1+2: SIMPLEX_AUTO_ACCEPT was a no-op two layers deep. The
request stayed pending, and the one message a contact request carries
still arrived - so the gateway logged an unauthorized user for a contact
that could never be answered, and its pairing-code reply had no
connection to travel back over.

The failure was also silent: the call discarded _send_command's return
value, so the chatCmdError never reached the log. Both the error and the
lost-reply case are logged now.

Note auto-accept is live-only. connect() starts a listener and nothing
else - there is no startup sweep - so requests stranded by these bugs stay
stranded and must be re-sent from the peer.

Still present in upstream v2026.9.14 on all three counts (v2026.7.20 to
v2026.8.16 identical); no branch has ever contained "/_accept", and no
test in tests/gateway/test_simplex_plugin.py names accept. Introduced by
0c2e81df0 "feat(simplex): groups, native attachments, text batching,
auto-accept". v2026.9.14 moved dispatch into an _EVENT_HANDLERS table
keyed on the event tag, still with "contactRequest" as the only key, and
into per-event _on_* handlers; this patch is rebased onto that layout.

Upstream, same silent-failure class, already fixed twice on the SEND path:
3a04d9c4d and eb048772f, "use structured /_send ... to prevent silent
drops". Accept was never revisited.

